# lap: a lap joint (decision C22). The chip goes in the vise legs up,
# dead-bug. The bending rig bends the resistor's lead 90 degrees 12 mm
# from its body and the rig's shear cuts it, leaving a bent end of about
# 4 mm; the arm lays that end alongside pin 3, touching it and pointing
# down the leg toward the chip, a 3.2 mm lap; then it is soldered. Two
# parallel pieces of metal soldered for 1/8 inch hold far better than a
# lead's end against a leg: inspect gives the lap. Last, the stage tilts
# the work so the microscope sees the lap from the side.
reset circuit=lap
tool A tweezers
pick A U1 grasp=ends
place A U1 at=0,0,-24 rpy=180,0,90
vise close
release A U1
pick A R1 grasp=body
lift A mm=60
insert A on=R1.1 at=12
form angle=90
lift A mm=30
shear A on=R1.1 at=17.2
lift A mm=60
bring A R1.1 to=U1.3.tip along=-0.934,0.356,0 lap=3.2
pinch P1 on=R1.1 at=3
release A R1
lift A mm=60
present U1.3+R1.1 at=S1
scope aim=U1.3+R1.1 zoom=8
touch S1 at=U1.3+R1.1 dwell=3 temp=400
feed S1 mm=2 rate=1
back S1
wait until=U1.3+R1.1 below=100
inspect U1.3+R1.1
unpinch P1
park P1
stage tilt=60
scope aim=U1.3+R1.1 zoom=10
